  urldate = {2024-04-16},
  abstract = {Mesoplodon currently comprises 15 species of beaked whales, making it by far the most diverse cetacean genus. Most mesoplodonts are rarely seen and many fewer identified at sea, and some appear to be quite rare. All are deep divers and suction feeders taking mainly mesoplagic fish and squid. They are small whales ranging in size from 3.9 to 6.2m and are found around the world in offshore waters from the subarctic to the subantarctic. Only adult males have teeth that erupt above the gumline; these comprise a single pair, whose size, shape, and placement in the lower jaw is diagnostic for the various species. Males use their teeth as tusks to fight for access to breeding females, and older males are often heavily scarred with long, linear tooth-rake marks.},
