  urldate = {2018-06-18},
  abstract = {The vocal repertoire of white whales, Delphinapterus leucas, summering in Cunningham Inlet, Northwest Territories. Can. J. Zool. 64: 407-4.15. The underwater vocalizations of white whales, Delphinapterus leucas, summering at Cunningham Inlet, Northwest Territories, were recorded from mid-July to mid-August 198 1 to 1983. A total of 807 tonal calls (whistles) were classified into 16 contour types. The following acoustic parameters were measured for each whistle: minimum, maximum, and mean frequency of the fundamental, contour or shape of the fundamental, duration, and the slope of the frequency changes during the call. Some 436 pulsed calls were classified into three major categories: click series, pulsed tones, and noisy vocalizations. Acoustic parameters measured for each of these calls included pulse repetition rate, range and mean frequency of the call, and duration. Results show that the whistle repertoire of white whales is more varied than has been previously reported. Mean frequencies for the whistle contour types ranged from 2.0 to 5.9 kHz; mean duration ranged from 0.25 to 1.95 s. Although whistles were the most commonly emitted type of vocalization, pulsed tones and noisy vocalizations made up a significant proportion of the white whales' vocal repertoire. The mean pulse repetition rate of pulsed tones ranged from 203.9 to 1289.0 pulses/s. There does not appear to be any between-year variation in the vocal repertoire of these white whales. SJARE, B. L., et T. G. SMITH. 1986. The vocal repertoire of white whales, Delphinapterus leucas, summering in Cunningham Inlet, Northwest Territories. Can. J. Zool. 64: 407-415. Les signaux acoustiques sous-marins des bklugas, Delphinapterus leucas estivant dans l'estuaire de Cunningham Inlet, Territoires du Nord-Ouest, ont kt6 ktudiks de la mi-juillet a la mi-aofit, de 1981 a 1983. Un total de 807 signaux tonals (sifflements) ont kt6 classks en 16 types d'aprks leur forme. Pour chaque sifflement, nous avons mesurk les paramktres suivants: les frkquences minimum, maximum et moyenne du sifflement de base, le contour ou la forme de la frkquence du sifflement de base, la durke et la pente des changements de frkquence durant le signal. Nous avons classifik 436 signaux a pulsations dans trois catkgories majeures: les skries de clics, les sons pulsatiles et les signaux bruyants. Nous avons aussi mesurk les paramktres acoustiques suivants: le taux de rkpktition, l'amplitude, la frkquence moyenne et la durke des signaux. Nos rksultats indiquent que le rkpertoire des sifflements du bkluga est plus riche que ce qui a kt6 dkcrit prkckdemment. Les frkquences moyennes des diffkrents types ont kt6 kvalukes a 2,O-5,9 kHz et la durke moyenne, a 0,25-1,95 s. Quoique les sifflements se soient avkrks les signaux les plus frkquents, les sons pulsatiles et les signaux bruyants reprksentent une proportion importante du rkpertoire. Le taux moyen de rkpktition des signaux a pulsations varie de 203,9 a 1289,O pulsations/s. Nous n'avons pas obtenu de changement dans le rkpertoire entre les deux annkes d'ktude.},
