  abstract = {The external measurements of 211 short-finned pilot whales off the Pacific coast of Japan and the observation of the pigmentation of some of those individuals are analyzed. They have pigmentation pattern fundamentally common to Globicephala. The growth of the trunk is characterized by the highest growth rate of rostrum portion in fetal stage and that of the region between umbilicus and anus in postnatal stage. On some appendages, the change of growth pattern occurs at parturition and/or after the attainment of sexual maturity of male. G. macrorhynchus is morphologically different from G. melaena in smaller size of body and shorter flipper and tail region.}
